      "writtenOn": "2025-12-19T13:23:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "How can you guarantee that the driver returned -ENOMEM because of a failed allocation and that `hyp_alloc_errno()` isn\u0027t just some stale old value?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 109,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 109,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "07acffc68fa9109494d4c812f51608f36b4aadf6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "46f74302_a7fa6915",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/iommu/pviommu.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 109,
      "author": {
        "id": 1965911
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-12-19T13:36:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That\u0027s a bit unlikely as errno is per cpu. Which means that the driver failed to alloc memory before and ignored it.\n\nBut in that case it won\u0027t be really a problem, the vCPU will exit anyway service this request and any other request in the page.\nAnd repeat the hypercall.\n\nOtherwise, we can clear `errno` before the pvIOMMU HVCs.",
      "parentUuid": "c1c08bd7_c1e17941",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 109,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 109,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "07acffc68fa9109494d4c812f51608f36b4aadf6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0ec44709_c869337d",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/iommu/pviommu.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 109,
      "author": {
        "id": 1951687
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-12-19T13:48:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Which means that the driver failed to alloc memory before and ignored it.\n\nTechnically, a CPU can run a HVC, hyp_alloc() fails and then alloc_errno() is set. Goes back to host but then it gets resched on a different CPU.\n\nThe best long term solution would probably to have a hyp_alloc() dedicated errno. I plan to introduce something like this for the host stage-2 ENOMEM , so that ENOMEM doesn\u0027t mean too many different things :-) \n\nBut at worst here this would over-allocate for hyp_alloc()?",
      "parentUuid": "46f74302_a7fa6915",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 109,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 109,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "07acffc68fa9109494d4c812f51608f36b4aadf6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
